WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.820
For many agencies the target is years
away: acquisition, budget cycles,

2
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:08.850
site logistics, and the same
staff on three other deadlines.

3
00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:10.375
That interval isn't empty.

4
00:00:10.375 --> 00:00:14.504
Four of the six things a branch edge
provides are partly available now,

5
00:00:14.504 --> 00:00:16.925
like path measurement and stable egress.

6
00:00:16.925 --> 00:00:20.605
And there's a fork coming
whether you plan for it or not:

7
00:00:20.605 --> 00:00:25.288
a directive requires end-of-support
edge devices out by August 2027.

8
00:00:25.288 --> 00:00:29.388
Replace like for like, and you've closed
the architecture question for years.

9
00:00:29.388 --> 00:00:32.580
Write the target attributes
into that purchase instead;

10
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:35.162
it costs almost nothing
at requirements time.

11
00:00:35.162 --> 00:00:36.980
Finally, proving it paid.
